{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>El</b> — thus may He help us to correct the causes, that He not incline it [the heart] to an evil matter." "<b>la'hit'olel olot</b> — that there be among them some wicked man, with men who practice iniquity." "<b>uval ekhaleim</b> — like <b>al tokhal et lekhem ra ayin</b> (Proverbs 23:6), and its meaning is: eat."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 141, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:25.848185821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}